# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Sivan Agreement Vault · environment
#
# Copy to .env and fill in. .env is gitignored; never commit a real key.
#
#     cp .env.example .env
#
# Nothing here is read at test time. `npx hardhat test` and `forge test` run
# against a local chain and need none of these. This file is only for deploying
# to Alfajores or Celo mainnet.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────


# ── DEPLOYER ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The key that signs the deployment. It becomes the initial owner of the vault.
#
# Use a FRESH key for testnet. Do not reuse a key that holds mainnet funds, and
# do not reuse your personal wallet: the deployer ends up owning a contract that
# can pause settlement and re-price fees.
#
# Generate one:
#     cast wallet new                      # if you have Foundry
#     node -e "console.log(require('ethers').Wallet.createRandom().privateKey)"
#
# Fund it with Alfajores CELO from https://faucet.celo.org
# No 0x prefix is required; both forms work.
DEPLOYER_PRIVATE_KEY=


# ── WHO RECEIVES MONEY, AND WHO SIGNS FOR DELIVERY ───────────────────────────
# SIVAN_FEE_COLLECTOR   receives the protocol fee on every release.
# SIVAN_AGENT_ATTESTER  the address whose EIP-712 signature the vault accepts as
#                       proof a deliverable was verified (ERC-8004 agent #9827).
#
# On Celo MAINNET the deploy script REFUSES to run unless both are set. Leaving
# them unset defaults them to the deployer, which puts protocol revenue and the
# attestation authority on a hot deploy key. That is a real mistake rather than
# a convenience, so the script stops rather than warns.
#
# These should be separate addresses from each other and from the deployer.
# Ideally the fee collector is a multisig.
SIVAN_FEE_COLLECTOR=
SIVAN_AGENT_ATTESTER=

# ERC-8004 agent id the attester signs on behalf of. Defaults to 9827.
SIVAN_AGENT_ID=9827


# ── RPC ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Celo Sepolia testnet (npm run deploy:sepolia).
CELO_SEPOLIA_RPC_URL=https://forno.celo-sepolia.celo-testnet.org
CELO_SEPOLIA_CHAIN_ID=11142220
CELO_SEPOLIA_EXPLORER_URL=https://celo-sepolia.blockscout.com
CELO_SEPOLIA_USDC=0x01C5C0122039549AD1493B8220cABEdD739BC44E

CELO_RPC_URL=https://forno.celo.org
CELO_ALFAJORES_RPC_URL=https://alfajores-forno.celo-testnet.org


# ── TESTNET TOKEN ADDRESSES ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# USDC IS THE PRIMARY ASSET. It is tested first, then cUSD, then USDT.
#
# The mainnet addresses are hardcoded in scripts/deploy.js because each was read
# back from Celo with symbol() and decimals() before being committed. The
# Alfajores USDC address is NOT hardcoded because no Alfajores RPC was reachable
# to verify it the same way, and a guessed constant in a token allowlist is
# worse than an omission: the vault would accept a token nobody intended, and
# nobody notices until a deposit lands.
#
# Set it here and the deploy script verifies it on chain, lists it first, and
# skips it with a message if it does not answer symbol().
#
# Find the current address in Circle's docs or on the Celo token list, then
# sanity check it yourself:
#     cast call <address> "symbol()(string)"   --rpc-url $CELO_ALFAJORES_RPC_URL
#     cast call <address> "decimals()(uint8)"  --rpc-url $CELO_ALFAJORES_RPC_URL
ALFAJORES_USDC=
ALFAJORES_USDT=

# cUSD on Alfajores is already hardcoded in the deploy script:
#   0x874069Fa1Eb16D44d622F2e0Ca25eeA172369bC1


# ── VERIFICATION ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Celoscan API key, so the source is published alongside the deployed bytecode.
# Free from https://celoscan.io/myapikey
#
# Worth doing. An unverified contract is a black box to anyone evaluating it,
# and a verified one on Celoscan is the single most useful artifact you can show
# for this work.
CELOSCAN_API_KEY=


# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# DEPLOYING
#
#   Testnet:
#     ALFAJORES_USDC=0x... npx hardhat run scripts/deploy.js --network alfajores
#
#   Mainnet (refuses without a fee collector and attester):
#     npx hardhat run scripts/deploy.js --network celo
#
# The script verifies every token on chain before listing it, seeds the
# allowlist in one transaction, then asserts the allowlist actually engaged.
# Without that last check it could report success while leaving the vault
# permissive, which is the exact hole the allowlist exists to close.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
